# What never goes to a remote.
#
# Two kinds of thing are kept out of git here: what belongs to whoever runs
# this installation - their music, their library state, their configuration -
# and what belongs to the private half of the project. Everything else is the
# application, and the application is meant to be read.
#
# One thing this file cannot do, and it matters more than anything it can:
# ignoring a file does not remove it from a repository that already tracked
# it, and untracking one does not remove it from the history it is already in.
# The public release is therefore built, not filtered - `npm run build:public`
# copies an allowlist into public-release/dist, and that directory is what is
# published, into a new and empty repository.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
service-role*
*service-role*
*service_role*
secrets.json
secrets/
credentials/
private/
supabase-private/

# Music, wherever it is kept. The source of truth for audio is the disk it is
# already on, and no copy of it belongs in a repository.
audio/
songs/
music/
local-media/
user-media/
uploads/
*.mp3
*.flac
*.wav
*.m4a
*.aac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.webm

# Local library index and cache (fully rebuildable)
.spotifie/
**/.spotifie/

# Local user data / runtime state
data/
local-state/
user-state/
users/
runtime-data/
users.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Generated caches, logs, temp
.cache/
cache/
caches/
.parcel-cache/
dist/
build/
dist-private/
build-private/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
tmp/
temp/
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/

# The built public release. Generated by "npm run build:public" and published
# by copying it into a separate repository - never committed here.
public-release/dist/

# Backups and archives, which are how a private file usually escapes
backup/
backups/
*.bak
*.backup
*.old
*.orig
*.tmp
*_backup.*
*_copy.*
*_old.*
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.7z
*.rar

# Anything named as private, and any dump of it
*.private
*.secret
*.local
dump.sql
*.dump

# The private half of the project: the administrator's pages and the script
# behind them. They are absent from every public build by construction - the
# release is an allowlist and they are not on it - and they are named here so
# a copy of one cannot arrive in a repository by being dropped in a folder.
admin.html
admin-dashboard.html
admin-login.html
admin.js
admin.css
admin/
admin-assets/
private-admin/

# How production is deployed from this private tree. It names the private
# build and the Cloudflare setting an operator must change, so it is an
# operator's document, never part of the public release or the public README.
DEPLOYMENT.private.md
# Internal QA and release reports.
*.private.md

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Wrangler local state, generated by "wrangler dev".
.wrangler/

# Desktop shell: the frontend written by npm run build:desktop, and what
# Cargo and Tauri generate. Rebuilt on every build; never committed.
desktop/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Android app: the frontend written by npm run build:mobile. The Android
# project's own generated output is ignored by android/.gitignore.
mobile/

# Generated admin dashboard document, written by the release build
# (npm run build:public / npm run build:production). Never committed: it is
# regenerated locally, and a production build inlines the private admin script
# into it.
worker/generated/

# Android release signing. The keystore and anything holding its passwords
# live outside this repository (see P16_ANDROID_SIGNING.private.md); these
# patterns are the safety net if one is ever copied in by mistake.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties
signing.properties
*.aab

# Signed release artifacts kept for provenance. These are the builds that were
# actually published, with the records that describe them; they are large, they
# are binaries, and a repository is not where they belong. Keep the folder -
# never delete it - but never commit it either.
release-backup/

# The owner's own note of secrets and recovery detail. It lives outside this
# repository; this entry exists so a copy dropped in by mistake is never
# committed.
spotiie-secrets.md
spotifie-secrets.md

# Claude Code local tooling (launch configs and local settings), like .vscode/.
.claude/

# Supabase CLI local link state (machine-specific, never committed)
supabase/.temp/
